**Given:**

sin θ + cos θ = frac{{sqrt 3 - 1}}{{2sqrt 2 }}

**Concept used:**

sin²θ + cos²θ = 1

**Calculation:**

sin θ + cos θ = frac{{sqrt 3 - 1}}{{2sqrt 2 }}

⇒ (sin θ + cos θ)² = (frac{{sqrt 3 - 1}}{{2sqrt 2 }})²

⇒ sin ²θ + cos ²θ +2sinθ .cosθ = (frac{{3 + 1-2sqrt3.1}}{{8 }})

⇒ 1+2sinθ .cosθ = frac{{4-2sqrt3}}{{8 }}

⇒ 2sinθ .cosθ = frac{{4-2sqrt3}}{{8 }}-1

⇒ 2sinθ .cosθ = frac{{4-2sqrt3-8}}{{8 }}

⇒ sinθ .cosθ = frac{{-(sqrt3+2)}}{{8 }}

Now,

tan θ + cot θ = (sinθ)/(cosθ)+(cosθ)/(sinθ)

⇒ (sin²θ+cos²θ)/(sinθ.cosθ)

⇒ (1)/(sinθ.cosθ)

⇒ (1)/(frac{{-(sqrt3+2))}{{8 }}}

⇒ (-8)/({{(sqrt3+2))}{}}

⇒ (-8(sqrt3-2))/({{(sqrt3+2)(sqrt3-2))}{}}

⇒ (-8(sqrt3-2))/({{3-4)}{}}

⇒ (-8(sqrt3-2))/({{-1)}{}}

⇒ 8( {sqrt3 - 2} )

**∴ The required answer is 8( {sqrt3 - 2} ).**

